# nf9: vendor.weaver-service removed on purpose.
#
# The A-version ramdisk shipped the SPU flavour
# (android.hardware.weaver-service-spu-qti) with "class hal". Measured on
# nf8: init starts it from class_start hal before /vendor exists, and it
# aborts every run --
#     android.hardware.weaver-service-spu-qti: Check failed:
#         status == STATUS_OK (status=-3)
#     received signal 6
# i.e. a 5-second crash loop for the whole session, dozens of restarts,
# which only polluted the logcat window used to debug gatekeeper.
#
# The real vendor has no weaver manifest fragment and no weaver rc at all:
# on this platform weaver is served by the OneKeyMint HAL together with
# keymint (vendor.gatekeeper.is_security_level_spu=0). TWRP does not call
# the weaver HAL anyway -- it reads /data/system_de/0/spblob/<handle>.weaver
# directly and falls back to the secdis blob, which is what happens here.
